From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:37:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: allwinner: Add the A733 display engine
 top block

The first page of the A733 display engine holds the reset and the
clock gate of each display, the reset and clock gate of its MBUS port
and the mux that connects each display to a TCON. Until the reset of a
display is released, its mixer registers read as zero and ignore
writes. Nothing describes this block yet.

Add a binding for it. The block is a reset and clock provider for the
mixers: display n has its reset at bit 4n of the register at 0x0 and
its clock gate at bit 4n of the register at 0x4; the MBUS clock and
reset are bits 0 and 4 of the register at 0x8. It sits in the graph
between the mixers and the TCONs, as the TCON TOP does on the H6; the
reg of an output endpoint is the TCON's number in the mux. It takes
the DE bus matrix gate, the DE bus, module and MBUS clocks, the DE
reset and the DE_SYS power domain.

The user manual does not document the block. Register names and bit
positions are the vendor's; only the reset of display 0 is known to be
needed for register access. The TCON numbers of the mux are listed as
the vendor device tree has them (0, 1, 2, 4, 5); only 5 (TCON TV1) has
been read back on silicon. The MBUS clock and reset are held by the
block itself.

Not covered: the other registers of the page, which stay at reset.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board with a device tree that
uses this binding; the top block probes and dtbs_check reports nothing.

Assisted-by: LLM
